{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgsb2A3Ve6TBFsu2qjsbU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Repetitions still start from fake-capture connections, and overall strength fell sharply. The new SA_conn penalises an E=0 connection between two weak chains at 6 units (−36). The worse-performing v10 also penalised these heavily (5 units), while v8B used only 2. These are typically cut-point connections, which matter a lot, so v8B's combined self-atari stays the best structure. Before deciding where to go next, let me check v8B's losses for points lost while my net passed and the opponent kept playing.\n\n```python\nimport json, numpy as np\nexec(open('/work/build8.py').read().split(\"CC,F0O\")[0])\nd='/work/pass_9/'\nG=json.load(open(d+'games.json')); B=np.load(d+'boards.npy')\ndef area(b,col):\n    # tromp-taylor area for col\n    s=int((b==col).sum())\n    seen=np.zeros(81,bool)\n    for p in range(81):\n        if b[p]==0 and not seen[p]:\n            st=[p]; seen[p]=True; mem=[p]; bd=set()\n            while st:\n                x=st.pop()\n                for q in NB[x]:\n                    if b[q]==0 and not seen[q]: seen[q]=True; st.append(q); mem.append(q)\n                    elif b[q]!=0: bd.add(int(b[q]))\n            if bd=={col}: s+=len(mem)\n    return s\nfor gi,g in enumerate(G):\n    if g['result']>0 or 'two' not in g['end']: continue\n    me=1 if g['net_color']=='black' else -1\n    mv=g['moves']; n=len(mv)\n    fp=[m['ply'] for m in mv if m['by']=='net' and m['move']==81]\n    if not fp: continue\n    k=fp[0]\n    def diff(j): return area(B[gi,j],me)-area(B[gi,j],-me)\n    print(gi,g['opponent'][:2],g['net_color'][0],'mg',g['margin'],'first net pass ply',k,'of',n,'area diff at first pass',diff(k),'final',diff(n-1),'net passes',len(fp))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1774,"cache